{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/busybox","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:10.082Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/cbl-mariner/busybox/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/cbl-mariner/busybox/about"},"readme":"***Warning: Azure Linux 2.0 will reach its End of Life (EOL) on July 31st, 2025. After this date, it will no longer receive updates, security patches, or support, which could leave your systems vulnerable. We strongly recommend upgrading to an Azure Linux 3.0 image before July 31st, 2025.***\n\n## About\n\nThis repository contains the official busybox image for CBL-Mariner. CBL-Mariner busybox container is lightweight and provides a minimal attack surface.\n\nBusyBox combines tiny versions of many common UNIX utilities into a single small executable. It provides replacements for most of the utilities you usually find in GNU fileutils, shellutils, etc. The utilities in BusyBox generally have fewer options than their full-featured GNU cousins; however, the options that are included provide the expected functionality and behave very much like their GNU counterparts. BusyBox provides a fairly complete environment for any small or embedded system.\n\n### What is CBL-Mariner?\n\nCBL-Mariner is an internal Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. CBL-Mariner is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about CBL-Mariner, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is a busybox container?\n\nBusybox container has only 3 CBL-Mariner packages i.e., filesystem, glibc, and busybox. BusyBox packages together multiple, common UNIX utilities (or applets) into one executable binary. It helps you create your own Linux distribution, and our associated container image helps you deploy it across different devices.\n\nDue to the limited set of packages, busybox container has a minimized security attack surface as well as reduced noise from vulnerability scanners. This generally translates to a reduced overhead of patching vulnerabilities, allowing developers to focus on building their application. Lastly, the smaller size (~10MB) provides higher performance.\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `2.0`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of their corresponding images. Additional tags that are specific to Mariner build or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Run BusyBox shell\nDepending on which CBL-Mariner version you want to use, replace `<tag>` with one from the Featured tags.\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/busybox:<tag>\n\nFor example,\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/busybox:2.0\n\nThis will drop you into an `sh` shell to allow you to do what you want inside a BusyBox system.\n\n### Create a `Dockerfile` for a binary\n   \n    FROM mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/busybox:2.0\n    COPY ./my-static-binary /my-static-binary\n    CMD [\"/my-static-binary\"]\n\nThis Dockerfile will allow you to create a minimal image for your statically compiled binary. You will have to compile the binary in some other place like another container or use multi-stage build.\n\n## Support\n\nCBL-Mariner container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)\n\nThe CBL-Mariner distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-07-21T17:00:05.6382861+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"8.4M+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"1.35","digest":"sha256:81582a125ce597114f2458d5ad7db2af24c6c115f2ae51d87f812b7096a71424","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:02:34.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1.35.0-cm2.0.20260311","digest":"sha256:81582a125ce597114f2458d5ad7db2af24c6c115f2ae51d87f812b7096a71424","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:02:27.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1.35.0-cm2.0.20260311-arm64","digest":"sha256:de7a95dfc9c6f2bd12d1b6d8fb9ef3aa7bf7efd794e65bb471a581e4d33f1c99","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:02:19.0000000+00:00","size":813,"platforms":["linux/arm64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1.35.0-cm2.0.20260311-amd64","digest":"sha256:361c7e801327d10df7e557af35d5d2c642296f9061a495f93184f82e4874a6a8","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:02:14.0000000+00:00","size":813,"platforms":["linux/amd64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1.35.0-cm2.0.20260304","digest":"sha256:1f9a0ed21a05a3f5d630696fe4f641e996a42ce650190c74c20d6d5ab2c2b000","pushed":"2026-03-10T17:40:45.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1.35.0-cm2.0.20260304-arm64","digest":"sha256:315f29d55a8c08166c130